.TH MAINUAN-GESTAO-DRIVERS 1 "October 2026" "Mainuan 1.0 RC1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mainuan-gestao-drivers \- detect hardware drivers and confirm package changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mainuan-gestao-drivers
.RI [ test ]
.RI [ --debug ]
.RI [ --version ]
.RI [ --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists additional drivers using the shared driver detection backend.
Driver selections produce a preview of planned package changes.
Applying changes requires explicit confirmation of a revalidated plan.
PackageKit performs installation and removal; the session PolicyKit agent
handles authorization. No password is collected by this application.
This is the Qt6 interface of Mainuan Gestao de Drivers, release candidate 1.0 RC1.
The legacy GTK frontend and its privileged Broadcom helper are no longer shipped.
Driver switches may remove packages before installing replacements and are
not atomic. Failed operations trigger fresh detection, without automatic rollback.
No global autoremove or automatic restart is performed.
Read-only preflight checks kernel headers, DKMS, Secure Boot and pending MOK
enrollment. Unsupported signing flows are blocked before changes.
DKMS with Secure Boot requires the actual signing certificate to be identified
and specifically confirmed enrolled. Pending enrollment remains blocked.
No keys are generated, imported or enrolled by this application.
Package installation alone does not establish that a driver is active.
Read-only sysfs binding and module signature evidence refine activation states.
APT candidates and Ubuntu driver recommendations are respected for distribution
and third-party repositories. Driver changes are blocked in Live or unknown
sessions. Detection remains available without Internet or PackageKit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B test
Use fictitious devices for inspecting driver choices, confirmation and progress.
Applying changes in this mode only simulates them in memory; no packages or
drivers are changed on the system.
The scenario selector includes NVIDIA recommendations, Broadcom, kernel/header
checks and Secure Boot/MOK states without consulting host APT or firmware.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable detailed diagnostic logging without changing driver policy.
.TP
.B --version
Display the application version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Display command usage and exit.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The Help menu can copy a local diagnostic summary to the clipboard on request.
No automatic upload is performed.
